<article class="env-lemma" id="03C5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03C5">Lemma <span data-tag="03C5">39.20.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a href="/tag/02VG" data-tag="02VG">39.20.1</a>. Assume there is a scheme $M$, and a morphism $U \to M$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the morphism $U \to M$ equalizes $s, t$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the morphism $U \to M$ induces a surjection of sheaves $h_ U \to h_ M$ in the $\tau $-topology, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the induced map $(t, s) : R \to U \times _ M U$ induces a surjection of sheaves $h_ R \to h_{U \times _ M U}$ in the $\tau $-topology. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In this case $M$ represents the quotient sheaf $U/R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Condition (1) says that $h_ U \to h_ M$ factors through $U/R$. Condition (2) says that $U/R \to h_ M$ is surjective as a map of sheaves. Condition (3) says that $U/R \to h_ M$ is injective as a map of sheaves. Hence the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>